integral -- evaluate Hodge integrals
************************************

  * Usage: 
        integral(g, n, klp)
  * Inputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * klp, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial in
        the *note kappa: kappa,, *note lambda: lambda,, *note psi: psi,, and
        *note ch: ch, classes of the ring returned by *note hodgeRing:
        hodgeRing,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,

Description
===========

 This function computes top intersection numbers among tautological classes on
the moduli space of curves. The tautological classes include products of the
Mumford-Morita-Miller classes $k_i$, the cotangent line classes $\psi_i$, and
the Chern classes and Chern characters, $\lambda_i$ and $ch_i$ of the Hodge
bundle.

The function *note hodgeRing: hodgeRing, must be called previously with values
of g and n at least as large as those to be used.

Examples
========

 Here are a few examples illustrating the $\lambda_g$ formula [FP, Theorem 1],
$$\int_{{\bar M}_{g,n}} \psi_1^{a_1}...\psi_n^{a_n} \lambda_g=
|B_{2g}|(2g+n-3)!(2^{2g-1}-1) / (a_1!...a_n!2^{2g-1}(2g)!),$$ where $B_i$
represents the $i$-th Bernoulli number.

